# Anchored to the repo root ON PURPOSE. A bare `exports/` matches at any depth,
# which silently swallowed the whole app/exports/ PACKAGE — lead_export.py was
# never committed and so was never in the Docker image. Harmless while nothing
# in app/ imported it; a boot-time crash the moment main.py did.
/exports/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.deployed-sha
deploy/deploy.log
.claude/
.vscode/

# Raw Smartlead dumps behind a campaign postmortem: ~35 MB of lead CSVs (names,
# emails, phone numbers) and full thread transcripts. The postmortem .md and the
# derived dataset .json next to it are the deliverable and ARE committed; this is
# the intermediate scrape, regenerable from Smartlead, and git history is forever.
docs/campaign-postmortems/_raw/
